{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/997955-priming-or-the-limitations-of-prime-magic","id":997955,"title":"Priming, or the limitations of Prime Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-03T16:42:42-07:00","id":997955,"title":"Priming, or the limitations of Prime Magic","content":"So, back in 1e we had a very interesting feature that allowed Prime to Scourge Mana from objects, taking 1 mana per 3 size of the object damaging it in the process. Led me to think:<br /> a) can a Mage with Prime 3 channel Mana from something that is not tass?<br /> b) can a Mage channel Mana into a person and then use that Mana to do a Pattern Restoration on the subject?<br /> c) on that note, can a Mage Scourge the Pattern of another to steal Mana from it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T17:16:49-07:00","id":997968,"title":"","content":"Death allows you to scour someone for mana:<br /> Devouring the Slain, Page 130.<br /> <br /> Might be possible to creatively use Prime to scour people and objects like in 1e.<br /> I'd say base it on Devouring the Slain and adapt a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T17:21:08-07:00","id":997970,"title":"","content":"Prime/Matter, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T18:50:16-07:00","id":998008,"title":"","content":"Honestly, with the new reworking of Prime, I would prefer Matter primary or even exclusive on such a spell. Otherwise, the argument expands to any other arcana: drain a spirit/person/ghost/whatever else by sucking out its mana. Requiring Prime to lean on another arcana to loosen up some of its patterns before it can muck with them just seems fair.<br /> <br /> Though... a Prime effect to make a thing no longer representative of a Supernal truth does make sense. (e.g. Declare some object is not, currently, participating in &quot;Weapon-ness&quot;, and, for the duration, so it cannot deal damage in a directed attack. Maybe even declare an argument &quot;not Persuasive&quot; and it stops working to persuade anyone.) The same problem applies, to a point, though. Don't require another arcana, and you unlock purt near anything.<br /> <br /> Still, adjusting which eidos apply to a given pattern does seem to fit the purview of Prime pretty well. Adjusting those and even slurping the underlying mana out of them does seem like a rather Prime thing to do. Best balancing act I can come up with, then, is high enough ability in another arcana to change what it is (Weaving, arguably, though Patterning certainly) unlocks the ability to start altering the pattern as if its mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T01:16:06-07:00","id":998137,"title":"","content":"That said the justification for Death being able to do that is probably that it draws on the same principles that ritual sacrifice does. <br /> <br /> You can't sacrifice a chair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}